{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he shall sprinkle seven times before YHWH, in front of the parokhet.</b> Above, in the case of the anointed priest, it mentioned את פני פרוכת הקדש — 'in front of the parokhet of the Sanctuary.' A parable: to a king upon whom a province rebelled. If a minority rebelled, his retinue endures; if all of them rebelled, his retinue does not endure. So too here: when the anointed priest sinned, the sanctity of the Place still rests upon the Sanctuary; but when all of them sinned, God forbid, the sanctity withdraws."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:49.633451959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}